Following Eq. \ref{eq:flux}, setting $W_i$ to 0.174 (see Sect. \ref{sec:intro}), we can estimate the initial mass of $^{44}$Ti from the $^{44}$Sc line flux reported above, finding $M_{44}=1.6\pm0.5 \times 10^{-4}$ M$_\odot$ (error bars at the $90\%$ confidence level). Our results are in remarkably good agreement with those obtained from the analysis of \textit{NuSTAR} spectra by \cite{bhm15}. On the other hand, our estimate of the $^{44}$Ti initial mass is significantly lower than that reported by \cite{glt12} on the basis of  the analysis of \textit{INTEGRAL} data.

