% At this point we do not know if it is true that in \emph{any} tangent category a $p$-carrable map is a $T$-submersion if and only if $\theta_f:f^{\ast}(TY) \to TX$ admits a linear section. While this is true in the cases we know, a general proof has resisted our attempts so far. In particular, we need to know one or two main results in order to generalize the arguments shown here:
