finite size systems which contain an integer number of eye-shaped unit cells.  Terminated in this way, the quantum states span a two-dimensional space, corresponding to the two topological sectors.  There are no other degrees of freedom

If we terminate the system in the middle of a unit cell, however, then we we must specify the configuration of the partial  unit cell.  The available Hilbert space will typically be spanned by two different 
%static (non-resonating) 
dimer configurations on that last partial cell, giving an extra spin-1/2 degree of freedom.
