In our protocol the gates always act on target atoms that begin in their ground state.  Thus we only need to define how they act on such states.  This gives us significant flexibility in gate design. Similarly, we only need to consider the control atom configurations which arise during our state preparation protocol.  
Since the gate operations are applied sequentially, some configurations will never appear. 
