\subsection{Creating the dimer state of Eye Model}
As a simple example, we first provide the sweeping protocol for the creation of the Rokhsar Kivelson state in the Eye model.

We label the Rydberg atoms in the Eye model as follows: each site is described by a binary array $\alpha=(n, i)$. Here, $n$ is the index of the plaquette to which the site belongs, ranging from 1 to $N$, where $N$ is the total number of plaquettes. The index $i$ ranges from 1 to 6. For the specific convention, refer to Fig.~\ref{fig:eyemodel}.

\begin{figure}[tbh]
    \centering
    \includegraphics[width=0.5\textwidth]{eyemodel.png}
    \caption{Caption for the Eye Model}
    \label{fig:eyemodel}
\end{figure}



In our creation procedure, we manipulate two sites at a time, turning on their dynamics and gradually change the parameter $\Delta$ to excite the Rydberg atoms. Then we turn off the dynamics, repeat the manipulation to the next two sites and keep this process until the whole state is prepared.

