Taking $J = (I^c \cup \{ i \}) \backslash \{ j \}$ gives $\theta_j - \theta_i \geq 0$. By taking $I = \{ 1, 2 \}$ or $\{ 3, 4, 5 \}$ and varying $i$ and $j$ we get $\theta_i = \theta_j$ for all $i, j$. Now setting $I = \{ 1, 2\}$ and $J = \{1, 3 \}$ gives $0 = \theta_4+\theta_5 -\theta_1 = \theta_4$. Hence all $\theta_i = 0$ which implies $\theta_x = 0 = \theta_y$. We conclude that $\theta = 0$. 
