\section{Conclusions}
%\noindent \textbf{5. Conclusions}

The work presents the analysis of international trade of the 8 most developed economies of the world. It is shown that the trade between them was not in a state of economic equilibrium. The relative equilibrium price vector turned out to be highly degenerate. A detailed analysis of the market shares occupied by each country is given.
