    \label{fig:histRM}
\end{figure}

The stellar mass function (bottom panel) aligns well with the data from \citet{Harvey:2025aa}. The observed points in the $z = 7.5$--8.5 bin match the $z = 8$ simulation results, indicating good agreement with model predictions. At higher redshifts, some deviations emerge, the observed number density is higher than we find within the \textsc{Phoebos} simulation, especially at $z \sim 12$. Nevertheless, the simulated data largely remain within their error margins. 

\begin{figure}
    \centering
