    Comparison of the $H_2$ and $H_3$ peak height ratios obtained from the analytical approximations of \citet{hu2001cosmic} (``H01''; thin blue), our polynomial emulator {\sc PolyCAMB-peak} (``Z25''; thick orange), and the true values from CAMB simulations (``CAMB''; dashed gray). 
    All curves are shown as functions of a single varying parameter, with the remaining cosmological parameters fixed at the pivot model.
